{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When a man of you brings an offering.</b> When he brings — it speaks of freewill offerings." "<b>A man.</b> Why is it said? Just as the first man did not bring from stolen goods — for everything was his — so you too shall not bring from stolen goods (Leviticus Rabbah)." "<b>The beast.</b> One might say even a חַיָּה is included — therefore Scripture says בָּקָר וָצֹאן." "<b>From the beast.</b> And not all of it — to exclude the one that mounted and the one that was mounted." "<b>From the cattle.</b> To exclude the one that was worked." "<b>From the flock.</b> To exclude the muktzeh." "<b>And from the flock.</b> To exclude the goring ox that killed; since it says below in the passage 'from the cattle' — which is not necessary — to exclude the terefah (Sifra)." "<b>You shall offer.</b> This teaches that two persons may volunteer an olah in partnership." "<b>Your offering.</b> This teaches that it may come as a voluntary offering of the congregation — it is the olah of 'maintaining the altar,' which comes from the surplus funds (Shevuot 12)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:39.074601673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}